dist/
node_modules/
*.tmp
*.log

# ── HAND-WRITTEN ENTRY POINTS INSIDE dist/ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `dist/` is a build-output directory, with three exceptions. These are PROGRAMS, not artefacts:
#
#   dist/harness-server.js   the standalone host
#   dist/watchdog.js         the two-state guardian
#   dist/harness.js          generated, but committed so `node dist/harness.js` works from a clone
#
# WHY THIS MATTERS: CI checked out the repository and ran `node --check dist/harness-server.js`,
# which failed with `Cannot find module` — because `.gitignore` excluded the whole directory and the
# two hand-written programs had never been tracked. The build produced `harness.js` only, so nothing
# recreated the other two. A file that is hand-edited but lives where only generated files are
# expected will always be lost this way.
#
# The negation lines below are the documented exception. The rule stays "dist/ is output"; these
# three names are the ones that are source.
!dist/
!dist/harness.js
!dist/harness-server.js
!dist/watchdog.js

# Local console home (demo graph + sessions written by scripts/serve-console.mjs)
.starfire-console/
.paradise-harness/
